{
  "summary": "Added automatic failed task recovery with exponential backoff - calculates backoff delay (1s, 2s, 4s... max 5min), sets next_retry_at timestamp, and maintains priority boost per retry. Implements proper retry scheduling instead of immediate re-queue.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "Exponential backoff",
      "reminder": "Use Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, retryCount), maxDelay) pattern for exponential backoff - prevents unbounded delays while allowing progressive backoff"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Retry scheduling",
      "reminder": "Store next_retry_at timestamp in database so scheduler can query only tasks due for retry, rather than re-processing all failed tasks"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Max retries",
      "reminder": "Check max_retries from task config to prevent infinite retry loops - compare retryCount against maxRetries before scheduling another attempt"
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "type": "potential_issue",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Task is reset to PENDING even when retryCount >= maxRetries - no check to stop retrying after max retries exhausted"
    },
    {
      "type": "observation",
      "severity": "info",
      "description": "next_retry_at is set but need to verify the scheduler queries this field when selecting tasks to execute"
    },
    {
      "type": "potential_issue",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "If max_retries is not set on task, defaults to 3 but no check stops at 3 - will keep retrying beyond default limit"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Add check: if retryCount >= maxRetries, set status to FAILED instead of PENDING",
    "Update scheduler query to filter: AND (next_retry_at IS NULL OR next_retry_at <= NOW())",
    "Consider adding a 'last_retry_at' timestamp for debugging"
  ],
  "praise": "Excellent implementation of exponential backoff. Good use of Math.min to cap delay at 5 minutes. Proper parameterized query. Clear variable naming.",
